      "raw": "<p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/67819#comment-67819\">As previously mentioned</a>, we wanted to get some feedback on the awards, especially as this was our first time. This thread is dedicated to the award categories, themselves; we&#39;ve created <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/general-thoughts-and-suggestions-forum-awards-2013-feedback-5279\">a separate thread</a> for thoughts and feedback on the process, how we did things, and the rest of it.</p><p>The award categories we used this year were:</p><ol><li><em>Inspiring Presence </em>(Morale Booster) &ndash; The forum member who, through positive attitude and kind heart, did the most to make the Greater Than Games forums a positive experience over the past year</li><li><em>Bolster Allies </em>(Funniest) &ndash; The forum member who was best at making people laugh and providing humorous moments over the past year</li><li><em>Truth Seeker </em>(Lore Master) &ndash; The forum member who has done the best job answering questions (rules, facts, mythology, etc.) and otherwise providing useful and accurate information over the past year</li><li><em>Harmony </em>(Top Debater) &ndash; The forum member who is best at rationally debating positions (without turning it into a fight) over the past year</li><li><em>Exceeded Expectations </em>(Top Contributor) &ndash; The forum member who contributed to the Greater Than Games community with tools and/or accessories the most over the past year</li><li><em>Bring What You Need </em>(Top Wikier) &ndash; The forum member who contributed most to the Greater Than Games wikis over the past year</li><li><em>Unique Capabilities </em>(Top Artist) &ndash; The forum member who created the best/most Greater Than Games-related art or fanfic over the past year</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What did you think of these award categories? What thoughts and suggestions do you have for future awards? How many do you think are appropriate? How many is too many?</p><p>Looking forward to reading your thoughts!</p>",
