      "raw": "<p>Alright, so we currently have forumite awards of:</p><ol><li><em>Inspiring Presence </em>(Morale Booster) &ndash; The forum member who, through positive attitude and kind heart, did the most to make the Greater Than Games forums a positive experience over the past year</li><li><em>Bolster Allies </em>(Funniest) &ndash; The forum member who was best at making people laugh and providing humorous moments over the past year</li><li><em>Truth Seeker </em>(Lore Master) &ndash; The forum member who has done the best job answering questions (rules, facts, mythology, etc.) and otherwise providing useful and accurate information over the past year</li><li><em>Harmony </em>(Top Debater) &ndash; The forum member who is best at rationally debating positions (without turning it into a fight) over the past year</li><li><em>Exceeded Expectations </em>(Top Contributor) &ndash; The forum member who contributed to the Greater Than Games community with tools and/or accessories&nbsp;the most (including wiki contributions) over the past year</li><li><em>Unique Capabilities </em>(Top Artist) &ndash; The forum member who created the best/most Greater Than Games-related art or fanfic over the past year</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p>And other awards&nbsp;of:</p><ol><li>Funniest Thread of the Year</li><li>Best Fan Fiction&nbsp;of the Year</li><li>Best Fan Art&nbsp;of the Year</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I tried to think of some other non-forumite awards, but haven&#39;t come up with any, yet. &quot;Best Thread of the Year&quot; seemed odd, as we&#39;ll all have different views on that kind of thing. Are there any other qualifiers and/or things that would make for interesting awards?</p>",
